 every day after noon.\n   - Remy either both goes to bed late and wakes up every day after noon and spends their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home, or they do not go to bed late and wake up every day after noon nor spend their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home.\n\n2.**Remy's Condition:**\n   - Remy either:\n     - Goes to bed late and wakes up every day after noon and spends their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home.\n     - Or does not go to bed late and wake up every day after noon nor spend their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home.\n\n3.**Logical Deduction:**\n   - If Remy spends their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home, then they do not go to bed late and wake up every day after noon (contradiction).Therefore, Remy does spend their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
