messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Karen will share "Stranger Things" to Lisa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', 'Let\'s break down the information given and analyze it step by step to determine if the statement "Karen will share \'Stranger Things\' to Lisa" is true, false, or uncertain.\n\n1.**"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show.**.\n   - This is given directly in the context.\n\n2.**If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.**.\n   - Since "Stranger Things" is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.\n\n3.**If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.**.\n   - Since Karen binge-watches "Stranger Things", she will download it.\n\n4.**Karen does not download "Black Mirror".**.\n   - This information is not directly relevant to "Stranger Things", but it helps us understand that Karen\'s downloading behavior is conditional on binge-watching.\n\nKaren will not share "Stranger Things" to Lisa.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
