utiful:.\n     - Beautiful → Popular.\n   - Therefore, Ben can be both blue and beautiful because being blue implies being unpopular, and being beautiful implies being popular. These are not contradictory.\n\n3.**Either Yellow or Ugly:**.\n   - If Ben is yellow, he might not be from The Simpsons (since being from The Simpsons does not necessarily mean being yellow).\n   - If Ben is ugly, he may still be popular.\n\n4.**Conclusion:**.\n   - Since Ben can be both blue and beautiful, the statement "Ben is either yellow and ugly or neither yellow nor ugly" is false because the first part (yellow and ugly) is not false, and the second part (neither yellow nor ugly) is false.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
