yee is in another country, they work remotely.\n\n6.**No managers work remotely from home.**.\n   - This means managers do not work remotely.\n\n7.**James is either a manager and appears in the company today or neither a manager nor appears in the company today.**.\n   - This means James is either a manager and in the company, or he is not a manager and not in the company.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement:.\n"If James is either a manager or in other countries, then James either has lunch at home and works remotely from home, or neither has lunch at home nor works remotely from home.".\n\n- **Case 1: James is a manager.If James is neither a manager nor in other countries, then James neither has lunch at home nor works remotely from home.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
